            <ArticleTitle>[Pancreatic hydatid cyst: an exceptional localization].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1056-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.arcped.2010.03.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pancreatic hydatid cysts are rare. They account for 1% of all hydatid cysts and are extremely rare in children. This may explain the problems diagnosing this condition. We report on a new case of pancreatic hydatic cyst in an 11-year-old girl who was admitted with a previous history of abdominal pain and jaundice. We discuss the diagnostic features of pancreatic hydatid cyst and therapeutic modalities.</AbstractText>
